      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Old_Town%2C_Edinburgh"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Royal Mile, coined early 20th century, slopes from Castle to Holyrood Palace, connecting historic sites.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Old_Town%2C_Edinburgh"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Narrow closes descend steeply from the main spine, some only a few feet wide.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Old_Town%2C_Edinburgh"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Edinburgh Castle dominates skyline from Castle Rock, a UNESCO World Heritage Site alongside the Old and New Towns.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
